-- title:
--   Run a prepared terminal test against exact original-value buckets
-- statement:
--   Fix $h,J,k$, a selected global output $q$, an arbitrary prefix list, and $N=\binom{(J-k)2h}{(J-k)h}$ using natural subtraction. Suppose the $N$ left/right terminal masks and selected cover data are stored correctly, together with original arrays and their exact physical buckets for keys $((x\bmod p+\sigma)\bmod m)$, where $m=\operatorname{modulus}(h,J)$ and the left shift is zero. Assume the stated disjoint preparation/scratch layout, terminal space and word budgets, depth $d+N+512hJ+8$, space fitting in a word, and word bounds for original values, target sums, and $N_LN_R$. The fixed program returns $r\in\{0,1\}$ with
--   $$
--   r=1\iff\text{some terminal candidate has both flags set and matching bucket positions }i,j\text{ with }R_j-L_i-a=0.
--   $$
--   It preserves memory below the preparation base and meets the preparation-plus-terminal-batch budget.
--
--   The test checks actual integer equality inside the selected physical fibers.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightReportingTerminalPrepared.lean#L50-L158

